cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use snai-int8 or its measurement series, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "snai-int8: int8 training of small transformer language models"
authors:
  - given-names: Sebastian
    family-names: Woratsch
    alias: komakeule57-maker
repository-code: "https://github.com/komakeule57-maker/snai-int8"
url: "https://github.com/komakeule57-maker/snai-int8"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
abstract: >-
  A research engine for int8 training of small transformer language models:
  int8 weights, integer matmuls in forward and backward with int32 gradient
  accumulation, and 8-bit Adam moments. In the default path, normalization,
  softmax, loss and the optimizer update are computed in float. With the
  switch SNAI_I8_GANZ=12, training runs entirely in integer arithmetic on the
  CPU, including attention softmax, RMSNorm, cross-entropy and an integer
  Adam update; a 0.37M-parameter model trained this way ends
  0.6-1.3 % above a paired float32 PyTorch baseline (3 seeds, 25,000 steps),
  and all four FPU rounding modes give byte-identical checkpoints. The
  engine is written in Nim with CPU (OpenMP), CUDA and OpenCL backends that
  are bit-identical to the CPU reference; the GPU paths are not integer yet.
  The repository also contains the research log: measurement series, each
  with a pre-registered criterion, recipe, raw values and verdict.
keywords:
  - int8 training
  - quantized training
  - stochastic rounding
  - small language models
  - transformer
  - Nim
